    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two are support classes), and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in the owner-create pipeline's audit step.\n\n**File changed:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`\n\nThe `AuditOwnerCreated` function now, after saving the owner:\n1. **Keeps the existing audit line** (unchanged human-readable log).\n2. **Emits an immutable structured event** via the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 a JSON object `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, serialized from an immutable `record OwnerCreatedEvent`.\n\nDesign details matching the spec:\n- **`seq`** is a `static AtomicLong` incremented per create, so it's monotonically increasing across all creates in the JVM (first create \u2192 `1`).\n- **Immutability** comes from the `record` type; the `event` marker is fixed to `OWNER_CREATED` via a compact constructor.\n- **Current primary identifier** is routed through a single `primaryIdentifier(owner)` helper that returns `customerCode` today. Its Javadoc marks it as the one place to switch when the customerCode is later unified into the `memberId`, so the event will then carry the memberId instead \u2014 exactly the forward-compatibility the spec calls for.\n- Serialization uses the project's Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper`), whose `writeValueAsString` throws only unchecked exceptions, so no `throws` clause is needed on the OfficeFloor function method.\n\n**Tests:** the target test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). Observed event in the log: `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.",
